{
  "title": "28: al-Qasas القصص",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nطٰسٓمٓ‏(1)\nTAA SIM MEEM.\nTa Seen Meem (T. S. M.)\nتِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِ الْمُبِيْنِ‏(2)\nTILKA AAYAATUL KETAABIL MOBEEN.\nThese are the verses of the Book which is manifest.\nنَتْلُوْا عَلَيْكَ مِنْ نَّبَاِ مُوْسٰى وَفِرْعَوْنَ بِالْحَقِّ لِقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(3)\nNATLOO A’LAYKA MIN NABAE MOOSAA WA FIRA’UNA BIL-HAQQE LEQAWMIYN YOAMENOON.\nWe recite unto thee from the accounts of Moses and Pharaoh, with truth, for a people who believe.\nاِنَّ فِرْعَوْنَ عَلَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَجَعَلَ اَهْلَهَا شِيَعًا يَّسْتَضْعِفُ طَآئِفَةً مِّنْهُمْ يُذَبِّحُ اَبْنَآءَهُمْ وَيَسْتَحْىٖ نِسَآءَهُمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(4)\nINNA FIR-A’UNA A’LAA FIL ARZE WA JA-A’LA AHLAHAA SHEYA-A’YN YASTAZ-E’FO TAAA-EFATAM MINHUM YOZABBEHO ABNAAA-AHUM WA YASTAHYEE NESAAA-AHUM, INNAHU KAANA MENAL MUFSEDEEN.\nVerily, Pharaoh exalted himself in the land and divided its people into parties, weakening a group among them, he slaughtered their sons and spared alive their women; Verily he was of the mischief-makers.\nوَنُرِيْدُ اَنْ نَّمُنَّ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ اسْتُضْعِفُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَنَجْعَلَهُمْ اَئِمَّةً وَّنَجْعَلَهُمُ الْوٰرِثِيْنَۙ‏(5)\nWA NOREEDO AN NAMUNNA A’LAL LAZEENAZ TUZ-E’FOO FIL ARZE WA NAJA’LAHUM AIMMATAWN WA NAJ-A’LAHOMUL WAARESEEN.\nAnd intend We to bestow (Our) favour upon those who were considered weak in the land, and to make them the Imams (guides in faith), and to make them the heirs,\nوَنُمَكِّنَ لَهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَنُرِىَ فِرْعَوْنَ وَهَامٰنَ وَجُنُوْدَهُمَا مِنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَحْذَرُوْنَ‏(6)\nWA NOMAKKENA LAHUM FIL ARZE WA NOREYA FIR-A’WNA WA HAAMAANA WA JONOODAHOMAA MINHUM MAA KAANOO YAHZAROON.\nAnd to establish them with power in the earth; and to show Pharaoh and Haman and their hosts to see from them what they did dread.\nوَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اُمِّ مُوْسٰٓى اَنْ اَرْضِعِيْهِ‌ۚ فَاِذَا خِفْتِ عَلَيْهِ فَاَ لْقِيْهِ فِى الْيَمِّ وَلَا تَخَافِىْ وَلَا تَحْزَنِىْۚ اِنَّا رَآدُّوْهُ اِلَيْكِ وَجٰعِلُوْهُ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(7)\nWA AWHAYNAA ELAA UMME MOOSAA AN ARZE-E’EH, FA-EZAA KHIFTE A’LAYHE FA-ALQEEHE FIL YAMME WA LAA TAKHAAFEE WA LAA TAHZANEE, INNAA RAAADDOOHO ELAYKE WA JAA-E’LOOHO MENAL MURSALEEN.\nAnd revealed We unto the mother of Moses, saying: “Give him suck; and if thou fearest for him, launch him on the River; and fear thou not, nor grieve thou; for We will return him unto thee, and make him one of the apostles.\nفَالْتَقَطَهٗۤ اٰلُ فِرْعَوْنَ لِيَكُوْنَ لَهُمْ عَدُوًّا وَّحَزَنًا ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِرْعَوْنَ وَهَامٰنَ وَجُنُوْدَهُمَا كَانُوْا خٰطِئِيْنَ‏(8)\nFALTAQATAHU AALO FIRA’UNA LEYAKOONA LAHUM A’DUWWAWN WA HAZANAA, INNA FIR-A’UNA WA HAAMAANA WA JONOODAHOMAA KAANOO KHAATE-EEN.\nAnd took him up Pharaoh’s people, that he might be unto them an enemy and a (cause of their) grief; (for) verily Pharaoh and Haman and their hosts were sinners.\nوَقَالَتِ امْرَاَتُ فِرْعَوْنَ قُرَّتُ عَيْنٍ لِّىْ وَلَكَ‌ ؕ لَا تَقْتُلُوْهُ ‌ۖ  عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّنْفَعَنَاۤ اَوْ نَتَّخِذَهٗ وَلَدًا وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(9)\nWA QAALATIM RA-ATO FIRA’UNA WA HAAMAANA WA JONOODAHOMAA KAANOO KHAATE-EEN.\nAnd said Pharaoh’s wife: “(Here is) a joy of the eye unto me and unto thee: slay him not: maybe he will be useful to us, or we will adopt him as a son;” But they knew not (what would Moses he to them).\nوَاَصْبَحَ فُؤَادُ اُمِّ مُوْسٰى فٰرِغًا‌ ؕ اِنْ كَادَتْ لَتُبْدِىْ بِهٖ لَوْلَاۤ اَنْ رَّبَطْنَا عَلٰى قَلْبِهَا لِتَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(10)\nWA ASBAHA FOWAADO UMME MOOSAA FAAREGHAA, IN KAADAT LATUBDEE BEHI LAWLAA AR RABATNAA A’LAA QALBEHAA LETAKOONA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd the heart of the mother of Moses became tranquilled; she was about to disclose it had We not strengthened her heart so that she might be of the believers (in Our promise)\nوَقَالَتْ لِاُخْتِهٖ قُصِّيْهِ‌ فَبَصُرَتْ بِهٖ عَنْ جُنُبٍ وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَۙ‏(11)\nWA QAALAT LEUKHTEHI QUSSEEHE, FABASORAT BEHI A’N JONOBIWN WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nAnd said she unto his sister, “Follow him!” And she watched him from afar: while they perceived it not,\nوَحَرَّمْنَا عَلَيْهِ الْمَرَاضِعَ مِنْ قَبْلُ فَقَالَتْ هَلْ اَدُلُّكُمْ عَلٰٓى اَهْلِ بَيْتٍ يَّكْفُلُوْنَهٗ لَكُمْ وَهُمْ لَهٗ نٰصِحُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA HARRAMNAA A’LAYHIL MARAAZE-A’ MIN QABLO FAQAALAT HAL ADULLOKUM A’LAA AHLE BAYTIYN YAKFOLOONAHU LAKUM WA HUM LAHU NAASEHOON.\nAnd already forbade We on him all fostermothers ere (his sister cometh there) and said: “Shall I guide you unto the people of a house who will take care of him for you, and they will (also) wish well of him.\nفَرَدَدْنٰهُ اِلٰٓى اُمِّهٖ كَىْ تَقَرَّ عَيْنُهَا وَلَا تَحْزَنَ وَلِتَعْلَمَ اَنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ وَّلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(13)\nFARADADNAAHO ELAA UMMEHI KAY TAQARRA A’YNOHAA WA LAA TAHZANA WA LETA’TAMA ANNA WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nSo We did restore him unto his mother that her eye might be refreshed and that she might not grieve, and that she might know that the promise of God is (always) true, but most of them know not.\nوَلَمَّا بَلَغَ اَشُدَّهٗ وَاسْتَوٰٓى اٰتَيْنٰهُ حُكْمًا وَّعِلْمًا‌ ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(14)\nWA LAMMAA BALAGHA ASHUDDAHU WAS-TAWAA AATAYNAAHO HUKMAWN WA I’LMAA, WA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nAnd when he reached the (age of) strength and was full-grown, We granted him wisdom and knowledge; Thus do We recompense those who do good.\nوَدَخَلَ الْمَدِيْنَةَ عَلٰى حِيْنِ غَفْلَةٍ مِّنْ اَهْلِهَا فَوَجَدَ فِيْهَا رَجُلَيْنِ يَقْتَتِلٰنِ  هٰذَا مِنْ شِيْعَتِهٖ وَهٰذَا مِنْ عَدُوِّهٖ‌ۚ فَاسْتَغَاثَهُ الَّذِىْ مِنْ شِيْعَتِهٖ عَلَى الَّذِىْ مِنْ عَدُوِّهٖۙ فَوَكَزَهٗ مُوْسٰى فَقَضٰى عَلَيْهِ‌  قَالَ هٰذَا مِنْ عَمَلِ الشَّيْطٰنِ‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ عَدُوٌّ مُّضِلٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(15)\nWA DAKHALAL MADEENATA A’LAA HEENE GHAFLATIM MIN AHLEHAA FAWAJADA FEEHAA RAJOLAYNE YAQTATELAANE, HAAZAA MIN SHEE-A’TEHI WA HAAZAA MIN A’DUWWEH, FASTAGHAASAHUL LAZEE MIN SHEE-A’TEHE A’LAL LAZEE MIN A’DUWWEHI, FAWAKAZAHU MOOSAA FAQAZAA A’LAYHE, QAALA HAAZAA MIN A’MALISH SHAYTAAN, INNAHU A’DUWWUM MOZILLUM MOBEEN.\nAnd he entered the city at a time when unvigilant were its people, and found he therein two men fighting: the one, of his own party; and the other of his enemies; And the one of his own party sought his help against the one who was of his enemies, and Moses smote him with his fist and passed (death) on him; Said (Moses): “This is of the Satan’s doing; verily, he is an enemy, an open misleader.\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ ظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِىْ فَاغْفِرْ لِىْ فَغَفَرَ لَهٗ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(16)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE ZALAMTO NAFSEE FAGH-FIR LEE FA-GHAFARA LAHU, INNAHU HOWAL GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nSaid (Moses): “O’ my Lord! Verily I have hurt mine own self, so grant Thou refuge to me!” So granted He refuge to him, (against his enemies); Verily, He is Oft-Forgiving, the All-Merciful.\nقَالَ رَبِّ بِمَاۤ اَنْعَمْتَ عَلَىَّ فَلَنْ اَكُوْنَ ظَهِيْرًا لِّلْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(17)\nQAALA RABBE BEMAA AN-A’MTA A’LAYYA FALAN AKOONA ZAHEERAL LILMUJREMEEN.\nSaid (Moses): “O’ My Lord! because of the grace Thou hast bestowed on me, never shall I be a supporter of the guilty.\nفَاَصْبَحَ فِى الْمَدِيْنَةِ خَآئِفًا يَّتَرَقَّبُ فَاِذَا الَّذِى اسْتَنْصَرَهٗ بِالْاَمْسِ يَسْتَصْرِخُهٗ‌ ؕ قَالَ لَهٗ مُوْسٰٓى اِنَّكَ لَغَوِىٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(18)\nFA-ASBAHA FIL MADEENATE KHAAA-EFAYN YATARAQQABO FA-EZAL LAZIS TANSARAHU BIL-AMSE YASTASREKHOH, QAALA LAHU MOOSAA INNAKA LA-GHAWIYYUM MOBEEN.\nAnd in the morn he, in the city, passed full of fear apprehending when lo! he who sought his help the day before, (again) crying out unto him for help. Said unto him Moses: “Verily thou art an open hot-head.\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَنْ اَرَادَ اَنْ يَّبْطِشَ بِالَّذِىْ هُوَ عَدُوٌّ لَّهُمَا ۙ قَالَ يٰمُوْسٰٓى اَ تُرِيْدُ اَنْ تَقْتُلَنِىْ كَمَا قَتَلْتَ نَفْسًۢا بِالْاَمْسِ ‌ۖ  اِنْ تُرِيْدُ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ جَبَّارًا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا تُرِيْدُ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُصْلِحِيْنَ‏(19)\nFALAMMAA AN ARAADA AYN YABTESHA BIL-LAZEE HOWA A’DUWWUL LAHOMAA, QAALA MOOSAA ATOREEDO AN TAQTOLANEE KAMAA QATALTA NAFSAM BIL AMS, IN TOREEDO ILLAA AN TAKOONA JABBAARAN FIL ARZE WA MAA TOREEDO AN TAKOONA MENAL MUSLEHEEN.\nAnd when he intended to seize him who was the enemy of them both, said he: “O’ Moses! Dost thou intend to kill me as didst thou kill one the day before? Intendeth thou nothing but thou shouldst be a tyrant in the land, and intendeth not thou to be of those who compromise.\nوَجَآءَ رَجُلٌ مِّنْ اَقْصَا الْمَدِيْنَةِ يَسْعٰى قَالَ يٰمُوْسٰٓى اِنَّ الْمَلَاَ يَاْتَمِرُوْنَ بِكَ لِيَقْتُلُوْكَ فَاخْرُجْ اِنِّىْ لَكَ مِنَ النّٰصِحِيْنَ‏(20)\nWA JAAA-A RAJOLUM MIN AQSAL MADEENATE YAS-A’A, QAALA YAA MOOSAA INNAL MALA-A YAATAMEROONA BEKA LEYAQTOLOOKA FAKHRUJ INNEE LAKA MENAN NAASEHEEN.\nAnd there came a man from the remotest part of the city, running, (and) said he: “O’ Moses! verily the chiefs are consulting to slay thee, Begone (from here at once)! Verily unto thee I am of the sincere advisers.\nفَخَرَجَ مِنْهَا خَآئِفًا يَّتَرَقَّبُ‌ قَالَ رَبِّ نَجِّنِىْ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(21)\nFAKHARAJA MINHAA KHAAA-EFAYN YATARAQQABO, QAALA RABBE NAJJENEE MENAL QAWMIZ ZAALEMEEN.\nSo, forth he went in fear, apprehending, (and) said he “O’ my Lord! Deliver me from the unjust people!\nوَلَمَّا تَوَجَّهَ تِلْقَآءَ مَدْيَنَ قَالَ عَسٰى رَبِّىْۤ اَنْ يَّهْدِيَنِىْ سَوَآءَ السَّبِيْلِ‏(22)\nWA LAMMAA TAWAJJAHA TILQAAA-A MADYANA QAALA A’SAA RABBEE AYN YAHDEYANEE SAWAAA-AS SABEEL.\nAnd when he turned his face towards (the land of) Midian said (Moses): “Maybe my Lord will guide me in the right path.\nوَلَمَّا وَرَدَ مَآءَ مَدْيَنَ وَجَدَ عَلَيْهِ اُمَّةً مِّنَ النَّاسِ يَسْقُوْنَ  وَوَجَدَ مِنْ دُوْنِهِمُ امْرَاَتَيْنِ تَذُوْدٰنِ‌ ۚ قَالَ مَا خَطْبُكُمَا‌ ؕ قَالَتَا لَا نَسْقِىْ حَتّٰى يُصْدِرَ الرِّعَآءُ‌ وَاَبُوْنَا شَيْخٌ كَبِيْرٌ‏(23)\nWA LAMMAA WARADA MAAA-A MADYANA WAJADA A’LAYHE UMMATAM MENAN NAASE YASQOON, WA WAJADA MIN DOONEHEMUM RA-ATAYNE TAZOODAAN, QAALA MAA KHATBOKOMAA, QAALATAA LAA NASQEE HATTAA YUSDERAR RE-A’AA, WA ABOONAA SHAYKUN KABEER.\nAnd when arrived he at the water of Midian, he found on it a group of men (watering their flocks) and found he besides them two women keeping back (their flocks); Said (Moses): “What aileth you?” Said the two (women): “We cannot water until the shepherds take away (their sheep from the water), and our father is very old.\nفَسَقٰى لَهُمَا ثُمَّ تَوَلّٰٓى اِلَى الظِّلِّ فَقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ لِمَاۤ اَنْزَلْتَ اِلَىَّ مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَقِيْرٌ‏(24)\nFASAQAA LAHOMAA SUMMA TAWALLAA ELAZ ZILLE FAQAALA RABBE INNEE LEMAA ANZALTA ELAYYA MIN KHAYRIN FAQEER.\nSo he watered (their flocks) for them, then retired he unto the shade, (and) then said he: “O’ my Lord! Verily of what Thou hast sent down unto me of the good, I stand in need\nفَجَآءَتْهُ اِحْدٰٮہُمَا تَمْشِىْ عَلَى اسْتِحْيَآءٍ  قَالَتْ اِنَّ اَبِىْ يَدْعُوْكَ لِيَجْزِيَكَ اَجْرَ مَا سَقَيْتَ لَنَا‌ ؕ فَلَمَّا جَآءَهٗ وَقَصَّ عَلَيْهِ الْقَصَصَ ۙ قَالَ لَا تَخَفْ‌ نَجَوْتَ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(25)\nFA-JAAA-ATHO EHDAAHOMAA TAMSHEE A’LAS TEHYAAA, QAALAT INNA ABEE YADO’OKA LEYAJZEYAKA AJRA MAA SAQAYTA LANAA, FALAMMAA JAAA-AHU WA QASSA A’LAYHIL QASASA, QAALA LAA TAKHAF, NAJAWTA MENAL QAWMIZ ZAALEMEEN.\nThen came unto him one of the two women walking bash fully; Said she: “Verily my father calleth thee so that he may recompense thee for what thou hath watered for us: So when came he unto him and narrated unto him his story, Said (the old man): “Fear thou not, thou art (now) secure from the unjust people\nقَالَتْ اِحْدٰٮہُمَا يٰۤاَبَتِ اسْتَاْجِرْهُ‌ اِنَّ خَيْرَ مَنِ اسْتَاْجَرْتَ الْقَوِىُّ الْاَمِيْنُ‏(26)\nQAALAT EHDAAHOMAA YAA ABATIS TAAJIRHO, INNA KHAYRA MANIS TAAJARTAL QAWIYYUL AMEEN.\nSaid one of the two (women): “O’ my father! Employ him, verily the best of those who thou canst employ is the strong (man) the trusted (one).\nقَالَ اِنِّىْۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ اُنْكِحَكَ اِحْدَى ابْنَتَىَّ هٰتَيْنِ عَلٰٓى اَنْ تَاْجُرَنِىْ ثَمٰنِىَ حِجَجٍ‌ۚ فَاِنْ اَتْمَمْتَ عَشْرًا فَمِنْ عِنْدِكَ‌ۚ وَمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ اَشُقَّ عَلَيْكَ‌ؕ سَتَجِدُنِىْۤ اِنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(27)\nQAALA INNEE OREEDO AN UNKEHAKA EHDAB NATAYYA HAATAYNE A’LAA AN TAAJORANEE SAMAANEYA HEJAJ, FA-IN ATMAMTA A’SHRAN FAMIN I’NDEK, WA MAA OREEDO AN ASHUQQA A’LAYK, SATAJEDONEE IN SHAAA-AL LAAHO MENAS SAALEHEEN.\nSaid he: “Verily, I intend to wed to thee one of these two daughters of mine on condition that thou servest me for eight years, and if thou didst complete ten (years) that will be a goodness of thine own accord; and I intend not to place any hardship on thee; Thou wilt find me, if God willeth, (one) of the righteous ones.\nقَالَ ذٰ لِكَ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكَ‌ ؕ اَيَّمَا الْاَجَلَيْنِ قَضَيْتُ فَلَا عُدْوَانَ عَلَىَّ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى مَا نَقُوْلُ وَكِيْلٌ‏(28)\nQAALA ZAALEKA BAYNEE WA BAYNAK, AYYAMAL AJALAYNE QAZAYTO FALAA U’DWAANA A’LAY, WAL LAAHO A’LAA MAA NAQOOLO WAKEEL.\nSaid (Moses) “Be it so between me and thee: whichever of the two terms I fulfil, there shall be no injustice unto me: And God, on what we say, is a witness.\nفَلَمَّا قَضٰى مُوْسَى الْاَجَلَ وَسَارَ بِاَهْلِهٖۤ اٰنَسَ مِنْ جَانِبِ الطُّوْرِ نَارًا‌ۚ قَالَ لِاَهْلِهِ امْكُثُوْۤا اِنِّىْۤ اٰنَسْتُ نَارًا‌ لَّعَلِّىْۤ اٰتِيْكُمْ مِّنْهَا بِخَبَرٍ اَوْ جَذْوَةٍ مِّنَ النَّارِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَصْطَلُوْنَ‏(29)\nFALAMMAA QAZAA MOOSAL AJALA WA SAARA BE-AHLEHI AANASA MIN JAANEBIT TOORE NAARAA, QAALA LE-AHLEHIM KOSOO INNEE AANASTO NAARAL LA-A’LLEE AATEEKUM MINHAA BEKHABARIN AW JAZWATIM MENAN NAARE LA-A’LLAKUM TASTALOON.\nAnd when Moses had fulfilled the term and was travelling with his family, perceived he on the side of the mount ‘Tur’ a fire; Said he unto his family: “Wait ye! Verily perceive I a fire, maybe I bring unto you from it some tidings or a brand (lighted) of the fire, so that ye may warm your selves.\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَتٰٮهَا نُوْدِىَ مِنْ شَاطِیٴِ الْوَادِ الْاَيْمَنِ فِى الْبُقْعَةِ الْمُبٰرَكَةِ مِنَ الشَّجَرَةِ اَنْ يّٰمُوْسٰٓى اِنِّىْۤ اَنَا اللّٰهُ رَبُّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ ۙ‏(30)\nFALAMMAA ATAAHAA NOODEYA MIN SHAATEIL WAATIL AYMANE FIL BUQ-A’TIL MOBAARAKATE MENASH SHAJARATE AYN YAA MOOSAA INNEE ANAL LAAHO RABBUL A’ALAMEEN.\nWhen came he unto it, (he) was called (by a voice) from the right side of the valley, in the blessed spot, from the Tree, saying: “O’ Moses! Verily I, am God, The Lord of the worlds\nوَاَنْ اَ لْقِ عَصَاكَ‌ ؕ فَلَمَّا رَاٰهَا تَهْتَزُّ كَاَنَّهَا جَآنٌّ وَّلّٰى مُدْبِرًا وَّلَمْ يُعَقِّبْ‌ ؕ يٰمُوْسٰٓى اَ قْبِلْ وَلَا تَخَفْ‌ اِنَّكَ مِنَ الْاٰمِنِيْنَ‏(31)\nWA AN ALQE A’SAAK, FALAMMAA RA-AAHAA TAHTAZZO KA-ANNAHAA JAAANNUWN WALLAA MUDBERAWN WA LAM YO-A’QQIB, YAA MOOSAA AQBIL WA LAA TAKHAF, INNAKA MENAL AAMENEEN.\nAnd saying: “Cast thou down thy staff;” And when he saw it moving as if (it were) a serpent, he turned back retreating and returned not: (then it was said unto him): “O’ Moses! Come thou forward and fear thou not! for verily thou art of those who are secure!\nاُسْلُكْ يَدَكَ فِىْ جَيْبِكَ تَخْرُجْ بَيْضَآءَ مِنْ غَيْرِ سُوْٓءٍ وَّاضْمُمْ اِلَيْكَ جَنَاحَكَ مِنَ الرَّهْبِ‌ فَذٰنِكَ بُرْهَانٰنِ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَا۟ئِهٖؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمًا فٰسِقِيْنَ‏‏‏(32)\nUSLUK YADAKA FEE JAYBEKA TAKHRUJ BAYZAAA-A MIN GHAYRE SOOO-IWN WAZMUM ELAYKA JANAAHAKA MENAR RAHBE FAZAANEKA BURHAANAANE MIR RABBEKA ELAA FIR-A’WNA WA MALAA-EH, INNAHUM KAANOO QAWMAN FAASEQEEN.\n(And now) pass thou thy hand in thy bosom, it shall come forth white (radiant) without evil: and close nearer thy sides against fear, and these be two proofs from thy Lord unto Pharaoh and his chiefs, verily they are a transgressing people.\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ قَتَلْتُ مِنْهُمْ نَفْسًا فَاَخَافُ اَنْ يَّقْتُلُوْنِ‏(33)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE QATALTO MINHUM NAFSAN FA AKHAAFO AYN YAQTOLOON.\nSaid (Moses): “O’ my Lord! Verily have I killed one of them, so fear I that they would slay me;\nوَاَخِىْ هٰرُوْنُ هُوَ اَفْصَحُ مِنِّىْ لِسَانًا فَاَرْسِلْهُ مَعِىَ رِدْاً يُّصَدِّقُنِىْٓ‌ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اَنْ يُّكَذِّبُوْنِ‏(34)\nWA AKHEE HAAROONO HOWA AFSAHO MINNEE LESAANAN FA-ARSILHO MA-E’YA RID-AYN YOSADDEQONEE, INNEE AKHAAFO AYN YOKAZZEBOON.\nAnd my brother Aaron, he is more eloquent than me in speech, so Thou send him with me as an assistant, to testify me; for fear I that they would belie me\nقَالَ سَنَشُدُّ عَضُدَكَ بِاَخِيْكَ وَنَجْعَلُ لَكُمَا سُلْطٰنًا فَلَا يَصِلُوْنَ اِلَيْكُمَا‌‌ ۛ ‌ۚ بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ ‌ ۛ‌ ۚ اَنْتُمَا وَمَنِ اتَّبَعَكُمَا الْغٰلِبُوْنَ‏(35)\nQAALA SANASHUDDO A’ZODAKA BEAKHEEKA WA NAJ-A’LO LAKOMAA SULTAANAN FALAA YASELOONA ELAYKOMAA, BEAAYAATENAA, ANTOMAA WA MANIT TABA-A’KOMAL GHAALEBOON.\n(God) said: “We will strengthen thy arm with thy brother, and We will give ye two an authority so that they reach not unto ye two, (go ye) with Our signs, ye two and those who follow ye two shall be the triumphants.\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ مُّوْسٰى بِاٰيٰتِنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ قَالُوْا مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّفْتَرًى وَمَا سَمِعْنَا بِهٰذَا فِىْۤ اٰبَآئِنَا الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(36)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHUM MOOSAA BE-AAYAATENAA BAYYENAATIN QAALOO MAA HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MUFTARAWN WA MAA SAMEA’NAA BEHAAZAA FEE AABAAA-ENAL AWWALEEN.\nSo when came unto them Moses with Our clear signs, said they: “This is nothing but a sorcery forged, and we heard not of it amongst our fathers of old.\nوَقَالَ مُوْسٰى رَبِّىْۤ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ جَآءَ بِالْهُدٰى مِنْ عِنْدِهٖ وَمَنْ تَكُوْنُ لَهٗ عَاقِبَةُ الدَّارِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(37)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA RABBEE A-A’LAMO BEMAN JAAA-A BILHODAA MIN I’NDEHI WA MAN TAKOONO LAHU A’AQEBATUD DAAR, INNAHU LAA YUFLEHUZ ZAALEMOON.\nAnd said Moses: “My Lord knoweth best who cometh with guidance from unto Him, and for whom shall be the good end of the abode; Verily, succeed not the unjust ones.\nوَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمَلَاُ مَا عَلِمْتُ لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرِىْ‌ ۚ فَاَوْقِدْ لِىْ يٰهَامٰنُ عَلَى الطِّيْنِ فَاجْعَلْ لِّىْ صَرْحًا لَّعَلِّىْۤ اَطَّلِعُ اِلٰٓى اِلٰهِ مُوْسٰى ۙ وَاِنِّىْ لَاَظُنُّهٗ مِنَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(38)\nWA QAALA FIRA’WNO YAA-AYYOHAL MALA-O MAA A’LIMTO LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYREE, FA-AW-QID LEE YAAHAAMAANO A’LAT TEENE FAJ-A’L LEE SARHAL LA-A’LLEE AT-TALE-O’ ELAA ELAAHE MOOSAA, WA INNEE LA-AZUNNOHU MENAL KAAZEBEEN.\nAnd said Pharaoh: “O’ Chiefs! I know not any god for you other than me, so burn for me O’ Haman, bricks of clay, and build for me a tower that I may mount up to the God of Moses, and verily I deem him to be one of the liars\nوَاسْتَكْبَرَ هُوَ وَجُنُوْدُهٗ فِى الْاَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ وَظَنُّوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ اِلَيْنَا لَا يُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(39)\nWASTAKBARA HOWA WA JONOODOHU FIL ARZE BEGHAYRIL HAQQE WA ZANNOO ANNAHUM ELAYNAA LAA YARJEO’ON.\nAnd prided he and his hosts in the land, without any right * and deemed they that they will not be returned unto Us.\nفَاَخَذْنٰهُ وَجُنُوْدَهٗ فَنَبَذْنٰهُمْ فِى الْيَمِّ‌ۚ فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(40)\nFA-AKHAZNAAHO WA JONOODOHU FANABAZNAAHUM FIL YAM, FANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUZ ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd We seized him and his hosts and We cast them into the sea; Behold then how (bad) was the end of the unjust ones.\nوَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ اَئِمَّةً يَّدْعُوْنَ اِلَى النَّارِ‌ۚ وَيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ لَا يُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(41)\nWA JA-A’LNAAHUM AIMMATAYN YAD-O’ONA ELAN NAAR, WA YAWMAL QEYAAMATE LAA YUNSAROON.\nAnd We made them Imams (leaders) who invite unto the (Hell) fire, and on the Day of Resurrection they shall not be helped.\nوَاَتْبَعْنٰهُمْ فِىْ هٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا لَعْنَةً‌  ۚ وَيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ هُمْ مِّنَ الْمَقْبُوْحِيْنَ‏(42)\nWA ATBA’NAAHUM FEE HAAZEHID DUNYAA LA’NAH, WA YAWMAL QEYAAMATE HUM MENAL MAQBOOHEEN.\nAnd We caused them to be followed in this world, by a curse; and on the Day of Resurrection they shall be of the loathed (ones).\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَاۤ اَهْلَكْنَا الْقُرُوْنَ الْاُوْلٰى بَصَآئِرَ لِلنَّاسِ وَهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةً لَّعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(43)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA MIM BA’DE MAA AHLAKNAL QOROONAL OOLAA BASAAA-ERA LINNAASE WA HODAWN WA RAHMATAL LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZAKKAROON.\nAnd indeed We gave Moses the Book after We had destroyed the generations of yore, (containing) clear arguments for man kind and a guidance and mercy, that happly they might reflect.\nوَمَا كُنْتَ بِجَانِبِ الْغَرْبِىِّ اِذْ قَضَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسَى الْاَمْرَ وَمَا كُنْتَ مِنَ الشّٰهِدِيْنَۙ‏(44)\nWA MAA KUNTA BEJAANEBIL GHARBIYYE IZ QAZAYNAA ELAA MOOSAL AMRA WA MAA KUNTA MENASH SHAAHEDEEN.\nAnd thou wert not on the western side (of Mount Sinai) when passed We unto Moses the commandment, nor wert thou one of the (eye) witnesses,\nوَلٰكِنَّاۤ اَنْشَاْنَا قُرُوْنًا فَتَطَاوَلَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْعُمُرُ‌ۚ وَمَا كُنْتَ ثَاوِيًا فِىْۤ اَهْلِ مَدْيَنَ تَتْلُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتِنَاۙ وَلٰكِنَّا كُنَّا مُرْسِلِيْنَ‏(45)\nWA LAAKINNAA ANSHAANAA QOROONAN FATATAAWALA A’LAYHEMUL O’MOR, WA MAA KUNTA SAAWEYAN FEE AHLE MADYANA TATLOO A’LAYHIM AAYAATENAA, WA LAAKINNAA KUNNAA MURSALEEN.\nBut We raised up generations (after Moses), and a long time passed upon them, and nor wast thou a dweller among the people of Midian, rehearsing unto them Our signs, but We were that sent thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad); (with the knowledge) (of the past).\nوَمَا كُنْتَ بِجَانِبِ الطُّوْرِ اِذْ نَادَيْنَا وَلٰكِنْ رَّحْمَةً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ لِتُنْذِرَ قَوْمًا مَّاۤ اَتٰٮهُمْ مِّنْ نَّذِيْرٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(46)\nWA MAA KUNTA BEJAANEBIT TOORE IZ NAADAYNAA WA LAAKIR RAHMATAM MIR RABBEKA LETUNZERA QAWMAM MAA ATAAHUM MIN NAZEERIM MIN QABLEKA LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZAKKAROON.\nAnd thou wert not on the side of the Mount ‘Tur’ when called We (unto Moses), but it is the mercy of thy Lord that thou warneth a people, unto whom no warner hath come before thee, that they may reflect.\nوَلَوْلَاۤ اَنْ تُصِيْبَهُمْ مُّصِيْبَةٌۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ اَيْدِيْهِمْ فَيَقُوْلُوْا رَبَّنَا لَوْلَاۤ اَرْسَلْتَ اِلَيْنَا رَسُوْلًا فَنَتَّبِعَ اٰيٰتِكَ وَنَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(47)\nWA LAWLAA AN TOSEEBAHUM MOSEEBATUM BEMAA QADDAMAT AYDEEHIM FAYAQOOLOO RABBANAA LAWLAA ARSALTA ELAYNAA RASOOLAN FANATTABE-A’ AAYAATEKA WA NAKOONA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd were it not so and should there befall unto them a calamity for what their (own) hands have sent before (them), then they would say: “O’ Our Lord! why didst Thou not send unto us an apostle then we would have followed Thy signs and had been of the believers\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ عِنْدِنَا قَالُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُوْتِىَ مِثْلَ مَاۤ اُوْتِىَ مُوْسٰى‌ ؕ اَوَلَمْ يَكْفُرُوْا بِمَاۤ اُوْتِىَ مُوْسٰى مِنْ قَبْلُ ‌ۚ قَالُوْا سِحْرٰنِ تَظَاهَرَا وَقَالُوْۤا اِنَّا بِكُلٍّ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(48)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHOMUL HAQQO MIN I’NDENAA QAALOO LAWLAA OOTEYA MISLA MAA OOTEYA MOOSAA, AWALAM YAKFOROO BEMAA OOTEYA MOOSAA MIN QABL, QAALOO SEHRAANE TAZAAHARAA, WA QAALOO INNAA BEKULLIN KAAFEROON.\nBut (now) when hath come unto them the truth from Us, say they: “Why is he not given the like of what was given unto Moses?” What! did not they disbelieve in what was given unto Moses before? They said: “(these are) Two sorcerers backing up each other;” and they said: “Verily we, in everything do disbelieve.\nقُلْ فَاْتُوْا بِكِتٰبٍ مِّنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ هُوَ اَهْدٰى مِنْهُمَاۤ اَتَّبِعْهُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(49)\nQUL FAATOO BEKETAABIM MIN I’NDIL LAAHE HOWA AHDAA MINHOMAA ATTABE’HO IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Bring ye then some (other) book from God which is a better guide than both of them, Torah and Qur’an), that I may follow it, if ye be truthful.\nفَاِنْ لَّمْ يَسْتَجِيْبُوْا لَكَ فَاعْلَمْ اَنَّمَا يَتَّبِعُوْنَ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ اَضَلُّ مِمَّنِ اتَّبَعَ هَوٰٮهُ بِغَيْرِ هُدًى مِّنَ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(50)\nFA-IL LAM YASTAJEEBOO LAKA FA’LAM ANNAMAA YATTABE-O’ONA AHWAAA-AHUM, WA MAN AZALLO MIMMANIT TABA-A’ HAWAAHO BEGHAYRE HODAM MENAL LAAH, INNAL LAAH LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nThen if they answer thee not, then know thou that they follow their own caprices; And who is more astray than he who followeth his own caprices without any guidance from God? Verily God guideth not the unjust people.\nوَلَقَدْ وَصَّلْنَا لَهُمُ الْقَوْلَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُوْنَؕ‏(51)\nWA LAQAD WASSALNAA LAHOMUL QAWLA LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZAKKAROON.\nAnd indeed We caused the Word (of guidance) to come unto them continuously, that they may be admonished.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ مِنْ قَبْلِهٖ هُمْ بِهٖ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(52)\nALLAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA MIN QABLEHI HUM BEHI YOAMENOON.\nAnd those whom We gave the Book before it, they are believers in it.\nوَاِذَا يُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِهٖۤ اِنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّنَاۤ اِنَّا كُنَّا مِنْ قَبْلِهٖ مُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(53)\nWA EZAA YUTLAA A’LAYHIM QAALOO AAMANNAA BEHI INNAHUL HAQQO MIR RABBENAA INNAA KUNNAA MIN QABLEHI MUSLEMEEN.\nAnd when it is recited unto them say they: “We believe in it, verily it is the truth from Our Lord, verily we were Muslims - (Submitters) (even from) before it (came)\nاُولٰٓئِكَ يُؤْتَوْنَ اَجْرَهُمْ مَّرَّتَيْنِ بِمَا صَبَرُوْا وَيَدْرَءُوْنَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ السَّيِّئَةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ يُنْفِقُوْنَ‏(54)\nOOLAAA-EKA YOATAWNA AJRAHUM MARRATAYNE BEMAA SABAROO WA YADRAOONA BILHASANATIS SAYYEATE WA MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM YUNFEQOON.\nThese shall be granted their reward twice for what they were steadfast, and they repel evil with good, and of the sustenance We have provided them with, they spend (in Our Way)\nوَاِذَا سَمِعُوا اللَّغْوَ اَعْرَضُوْا عَنْهُ وَقَالُوْا لَنَاۤ اَعْمَالُنَا وَلَكُمْ اَعْمَالُكُمْ سَلٰمٌ عَلَيْكُمْ لَا نَبْتَغِى الْجٰهِلِيْنَ‏(55)\nWA EZAA SAME-O’L LAGHWA A-A’RAZOO A’NHO WA QAALOO LANAA A-A’MAALONAA WA LAKUM A-A’MAALOKUM, SALAAMUN A’LAYKUM, LAA NABTAGHIL JAAHELEEN.\nAnd when hear they any vain talk, they withdraw from it, and say they: “For us shall be our deeds, and for you shall be your deeds, peace be on you, we desire not the (society of the) ignorants.\nاِنَّكَ لَا تَهْدِىْ مَنْ اَحْبَبْتَ وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ‌ؕ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(56)\nINNAKA LAA TAHDEE MAN AHBABTA WA LAAKINNAL LAAHA YAHDEE MAYN YASHAAA, WA HOWA A-A’LAMO BILMOHTADEEN.\nVerily, thou canst not guide whomsoever thou likest; but God guideth whomsoever He pleaseth, and He knoweth best those who follow aright.\nوَقَالُوْۤا اِنْ نَّتَّبِعِ الْهُدٰى مَعَكَ نُتَخَطَّفْ مِنْ اَرْضِنَا ؕ اَوَلَمْ نُمَكِّنْ لَّهُمْ حَرَمًا اٰمِنًا يُّجْبٰٓى اِلَيْهِ ثَمَرٰتُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ رِّزْقًا مِّنْ لَّدُنَّا وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(57)\nWA QAALOO IN NATTABE-I’L HODAA MA-A’KA NOTAKHATTAF MIN ARZENAA, AWALAM NOMAKKIL LAHUM HARAMAN AAMENAYN YUJBAA ELAYHE SAMARAATO KULLE SHAY-IR RIZQAM MIL LADUNNAA WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd they say: “If we follow the guidance with thee, we shall be driven out from our land” What! have We not established them in a sacred (and) safe precinct, unto which are drawn fruits of every thing? - a sustenance provided from unto Us; but most of them know not.\nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَرْيَةٍۢ بَطِرَتْ مَعِيْشَتَهَا ‌ۚ فَتِلْكَ مَسٰكِنُهُمْ لَمْ تُسْكَنْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا ؕ وَكُنَّا نَحْنُ الْوٰرِثِيْنَ‏(58)\nWA KAM AHLAKNAA MIN QARYATIM BATERAT MA-E’ESHATAHAA, FATILKA MASAAKENOHUM LAM TUSKAM MIM BA’DEHIM ILLAA QALEELA, WA KUNNAA NAHNUL WAARESEEN.\nAnd how many a town We did destroy, which exulted in its means of subsistence; So these their dwellings have not been inhabited after them save a little, and We are their heirs!\nوَ مَا كَانَ رَبُّكَ مُهْلِكَ الْقُرٰى حَتّٰى يَبْعَثَ فِىْۤ اُمِّهَا رَسُوْلًا يَّتْلُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتِنَا‌ ۚ وَمَا كُنَّا مُهْلِكِى الْقُرٰٓى اِلَّا وَاَهْلُهَا ظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(59)\nWA MAA KAANA RABBOKA MOHLEKAL KORAA HATTAA YAB-A’SA FEE UMMEHAA RASOOLAYN YATLOO A’LAYHIM AAYAATENAA, WA MAA KUNNAA MOHLEKIL QORAA ILLAA WA AHLOHAA ZAALEMOON.\nAnd thy Lord destroyeth not the towns until He raiseth in their Mother-(Town) (metropolis) an apostle, rehearsing unto them Our signs, and We destroyed not the towns except while their people were unjust.\nوَمَاۤ اُوْتِيْتُمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ فَمَتَاعُ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَزِيْنَتُهَا‌ ۚ وَمَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ خَيْرٌ وَّاَبْقٰى‌ ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(60)\nWA MAA OOTEETUM MIN SHAY-IN FAMATAAUL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA ZEENATOHAA, WA MAA I’NDAL LAAHE KHAYRUWN WA ABQAA, AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nAnd of whatever things ye have been given are only a provision of the life of this world and its adornment; and whatever is with God, is better and more lasting; What! do ye not then understand?\nاَفَمَنْ وَّعَدْنٰهُ وَعْدًا حَسَنًا فَهُوَ لَاقِيْهِ كَمَنْ مَّتَّعْنٰهُ مَتَاعَ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ثُمَّ هُوَ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ مِنَ الْمُحْضَرِيْنَ‏(61)\nAFAMAWN WA-A’DNAAHO WA’DAN HASANAN FAHOWA LAAQEEHE KAMAM MATTA’NAAHO MATAA-A’L HAYAATID DUNYA SUMMA HOWA YAWMAL QEYAAMATE MENAL MOHZAREEN.\nWhat! Is he then unto whom We have promised a goodly promise which he shall meet it, similar to him whom We have provided with the provision of the life of this world, then on the Day of Resurrection he shall be of those arraigned?\nوَيَوْمَ يُنَادِيْهِمْ فَيَقُوْلُ اَيْنَ شُرَكَآءِىَ الَّذِيْنَ كُنْتُمْ تَزْعُمُوْنَ‏(62)\nWA YAWMA YONAADEEHIM FAYAQOOLO AYNA SHORAKAAA-EYAL LAZEENA KUNTUM TAZ-O’MOON.\nOn that day will call (God) unto them and say: “Where are My partners whom ye were asserting?\nقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ حَقَّ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقَوْلُ رَبَّنَا هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ الَّذِيْنَ اَغْوَيْنَا ۚ اَغْوَيْنٰهُمْ كَمَا غَوَيْنَا‌ ۚ تَبَرَّاْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ‌ مَا كَانُوْۤا اِيَّانَا يَعْبُدُوْنَ‏(63)\nQAALAL LAZEENA HAQQA A’LAYHEMUL QAWLO RABBANAA HAA-OLAAA-IL LAZEENA AGHWAYNAA, AGHWAYNAAHUM KAMAA GHAWAYNAA, TABARRAANAA ELAYK, MAA KAANOO IYYAANAA YA’BODOON.\nThose against whom the sentence hath been confirmed will say: “O’ Our Lord! These are they whom we led astray: we led them astray even as we had been led astray ourselves: we declare unto Thee to be free (of them): They were not unto us worshipping.\nوَقِيْلَ ادْعُوْا شُرَكَآءَكُمْ فَدَعَوْهُمْ فَلَمْ يَسْتَجِيْبُوْا لَهُمْ وَرَاَوُا الْعَذَابَ‌ۚ لَوْ اَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(64)\nWA QEELAD O’O SHORAKAAA-AKUM FADA-A’WHUM FALAM YASTAJEEBOO LAHUM WA RA-AWUL A’ZAAB, LAW ANNAHUM KAANOO YAHTADOON.\nAnd it will be said (unto them): “Call ye your associate (gods)” so they called upon them, but they answered them not, and they shall see the chastisement, and would wish that they had been guided aright.\nوَيَوْمَ يُنَادِيْهِمْ فَيَقُوْلُ مَاذَاۤ اَجَبْتُمُ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(65)\nWA YAWMA YONAADEEHIM FAYAQOOLO MAA ZAA AJABTOMUL MURSALEEN.\nAnd on that day shall (God) call unto them and say: “What was it that ye answered the apostles (from Me)?\nفَعَمِيَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الْاَنْۢبَآءُ يَوْمَئِذٍ فَهُمْ لَا يَتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(66)\nFA-A’MEYAT A’LAYHEMUL AMBAAA-O YAWMA-EZIN FAHUM LAA YATASAAA-ALOON.\nBut the tidings shall that day be so confusing that they shall (even) ask not each other.\nفَاَمَّا مَنْ تَابَ وَاٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَعَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُفْلِحِيْنَ‏(67)\nFA-AMMAA MAN TAABA WA AAMANA WA A’MELA SAALEHAN FA-A’SAA AYN YAKOONA MENAL MUFLEHEEN.\nYet as to him who turned repentant unto God and believed and did good, maybe he will be among the successful (ones)\nوَرَبُّكَ يَخْلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُ وَيَخْتَارُ‌ؕ مَا كَانَ لَهُمُ الْخِيَرَةُ‌ ؕ سُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ وَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(68)\nWA RABBOKA YAKHLOQO MAA YASHAAA-O WA YAKHTAAR, MAA KAANA LAHOMUL KHEYARAH, SUBHAANAL LAAHE WA TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nAnd thy Lord createth whatever He willeth and (also) chooseth too; it is not theirs to choose; Hallowed is God and Exalted High is He (far) above what they join (with Him).\nوَرَبُّكَ يَعْلَمُ مَا تُكِنُّ صُدُوْرُهُمْ وَمَا يُعْلِنُوْنَ‏(69)\nWA RABBOKA YA’LAMO MAA TOKINNO SODOOROHUM WA MAA YO’LENOON.\nAnd thy Lord knoweth what concealeth their breasts and what they declare.\nوَهُوَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ‌ؕ لَهُ الْحَمْدُ فِى الْاُوْلٰى وَالْاٰخِرَةِ وَلَهُ الْحُكْمُ وَاِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(70)\nWA HOWAL LAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO, LAHUL HAMDO FIL OOLAA WAL AAKHERAH, WA LAHUL HUKMO WA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nAnd He is God, there is no god but He! His is all praise, in first and (in) the last, and His is the authority, and unto Him (only) ye shall be returned.\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكُمُ الَّيْلَ سَرْمَدًا اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ مَنْ اِلٰهٌ غَيْرُ اللّٰهِ يَاْتِيْكُمْ بِضِيَآءٍ‌ؕاَفَلَا تَسْمَعُوْنَ‏(71)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM IN JA-A’LAL LAAHO A’LAYKOMUL LAYLA SARMADAN ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE MAN ELAAHUN GHAYRUL LAAHE YAATEEKUM BEZEYAAA, AFALAA TASMA-O’ON.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “See ye? Had God made the night to continue on you until the Day of Resurrection, who is the god other than God that could bring light unto you; What! Do ye not then hear?\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكُمُ النَّهَارَ سَرْمَدًا اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ مَنْ اِلٰهٌ غَيْرُ اللّٰهِ يَاْتِيْكُمْ بِلَيْلٍ تَسْكُنُوْنَ فِيْهِ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(72)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM IN JA-A’LAL LAAHO A’LAYKOMUN NAHAARA SARMADAN ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE MAN ELAAHUN GHAYRUL LAAHE YAATEEKUM BELAYLIN TASKONOONA FEEH, AFALAA TUBSEROON.\nSay thou: “See ye?” Had God made the day to continue on you until the Day of Resurrection, who is the god other than God that could bring, night unto you, that ye rest therein? What! Do ye not then see?\nوَمِنْ رَّحْمَتِهٖ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ لِتَسْكُنُوْا فِيْهِ وَلِتَبْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(73)\nWA MIR RAHMATEHI JA-A’LA LAKOMUL LAYLA WAN NAHAARA LETASKONOO FEEHE WA LETABTAGHOO MIN FAZLEHI WA LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nAnd of His mercy He hath made for you the night and the day, that ye may rest therein, and that ye may seek of His grace, and that ye may give thanks.\nوَيَوْمَ يُنَادِيْهِمْ فَيَقُوْلُ اَيْنَ شُرَكَآءِىَ الَّذِيْنَ كُنْتُمْ تَزْعُمُوْنَ‏(74)\nWA YAWMA YONAADEEHIM FAYAQOOLO AYNA SHORAKAAA-EYAL LAZEENA KUNTUM TAZ-O’MOON.\nAnd on that day when He shall call unto them and say: “Where are My partners whom ye used to assert?\nوَنَزَعْنَا مِنْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ شَهِيْدًا فَقُلْنَا هَاتُوْا بُرْهَانَكُمْ فَعَلِمُوْۤا اَنَّ الْحَقَّ لِلّٰهِ وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(75)\nWA NAZA’NAA MIN KULLE UMMATIN SHAHEEDAN FAQULNAA HAATOO BURHAANAKUM FA-A’LEMOO ANNAL HAQQA LILLAAHE WA ZALLA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nAnd We will draw forth from every people a witness, and We will say: “Bring ye your proof; then shall they know that the truth is God’s, and shall depart from them what they used to forge.\nاِنَّ قَارُوْنَ كَانَ مِنْ قَوْمِ مُوْسٰى فَبَغٰى عَلَيْهِمْ‌ وَاٰتَيْنٰهُ مِنَ الْكُنُوْزِ مَاۤ اِنَّ مَفَاتِحَهٗ لَتَنُوْٓاُ بِالْعُصْبَةِ اُولِى الْقُوَّةِ اِذْ قَالَ لَهٗ قَوْمُهٗ لَا تَفْرَحْ‌ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْفَرِحِيْنَ‏(76)\nINNA QAAROONA KAANA MIN QAWME MOOSAA FABAGHAA A’LAYHIM, WA AATAYNAAHO MENAL KONOOZE MAA INNA MAFAATEHAHU LATANOOO-O BIL-U’SBATE OOLIL QUWWAH, IZ QAALA LAHU QAWMOHU LAA TAFRAH INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL FAREHEEN.\nVerily, Korah (Qarun) was of the people of Moses, but he rebelled against them, and We had given him of the treasures so much that its keys would have been a burden to a company of men of strength. When his people said unto him, “Exalt thou not, for God loveth not those who exult.\nوَابْتَغِ فِيْمَاۤ اٰتٰٮكَ اللّٰهُ الدَّارَ الْاٰخِرَةَ‌ وَلَا تَنْسَ نَصِيْبَكَ مِنَ الدُّنْيَا‌ وَاَحْسِنْ كَمَاۤ اَحْسَنَ اللّٰهُ اِلَيْكَ‌ وَلَا تَبْغِ الْفَسَادَ فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(77)\nWABTAGHE FEEMAA AATAAKAL LAAHUD DAARAL AAKHERATA WA LAA TANSA NASEEBAKA MENAD DUNYAA WA AHSIN KAMAA AHSANAL LAAHO ELAYKA WA LAA TABGHIL FASAADA FIL ARZ, INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL MUFSEDEEN.\nAnd seek, by means of what God hath given thee, the abode in hereafter, and forget not thy share in this world, and be good to others even as God hath been good unto thee, and seek thou not to mischief in the earth, Verily, God loveth not the mischief-makers.\nقَالَ اِنَّمَاۤ اُوْتِيْتُهٗ عَلٰى عِلْمٍ عِنْدِىْ‌ؕ اَوَلَمْ يَعْلَمْ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ قَدْ اَهْلَكَ مِنْ قَبْلِهٖ مِنَ الْقُرُوْنِ مَنْ هُوَ اَشَدُّ مِنْهُ قُوَّةً وَّاَكْثَرُ جَمْعًا‌ؕ وَلَا يُسْئَلُ عَنْ ذُنُوْبِهِمُ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(78)\nQAALA INNAMAA OOTEETOHU A’LAA I’LMIN I’NDEE, AWALAM YA’LAM ANNAL LAAHA QAD AHLAKA MIN QABLEHI MENAL QOROONE MAN HOWA ASHADDO MINHO QUWWATAW WA AKSARO JAM-A’, WA LAA YUSALO A’N ZONOOBEHEMUL MUJREMOON.\nSaid (Korah): “It hath been given unto me only for the knowledge I possess;” What! knew he not that God hath indeed destroyed before him of the generations that were mightier in strength than he and greater in hoarding (of wealth)? And the guilty (at the time of punishment) shall not be questioned against their faults.\nفَخَرَجَ عَلٰى قَوْمِهٖ فِىْ زِيْنَتِهٖ‌ؕ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ يُرِيْدُوْنَ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا يٰلَيْتَ لَنَا مِثْلَ مَاۤ اُوْتِىَ قَارُوْنُۙ اِنَّهٗ لَذُوْ حَظٍّ عَظِيْمٍ‏(79)\nFAKHARAJA A’LAA QAWMEHI FEE ZEENATEH, QAALAL LAZEENA YOREEDOONAL HAYAATAD DUNYAA YAALAYTA LANAA MISLA MAA OOTEYA QAAROONO, INNAHU LAZOO HAZZIN A’ZEEM.\nSo went forth he unto his people in his pomp; (And) Said those who aspired for the life of this world: “Oh! would that we had the like of what hath been given unto Korah, verily he owneth a great fortune\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ وَيْلَكُمْ ثَوَابُ اللّٰهِ خَيْرٌ لِّمَنْ اٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا ۚ وَلَا يُلَقّٰٮهَاۤ اِلَّا الصّٰبِرُوْنَ‏(80)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENA OOTUL I’LMA WAYLAKUM SAWAABUL LAAHE KHAYRUL LEMAN AAMANA WA A’MELA SAALEHAA, WA LAA YOLAQQAAHAA ILLAS SAABEROON.\nAnd those who were given the knowledge said: “Woe unto you! The reward of God is better for him who believeth and doeth good, but none shall attain it save the steadfast ones\nفَخَسَفْنَا بِهٖ وَبِدَارِهِ الْاَرْضَ فَمَا كَانَ لَهٗ مِنْ فِئَةٍ يَّنْصُرُوْنَهٗ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ الْمُنْتَصِرِيْنَ‏(81)\nFAKHASAFNAA BEHI WA BEDAAREHIL ARZ, FAMAA KAANA LAHU MIN FE-ATIYN YANSOROONAHU MIN DOONIL LAAH, WA MAA KAANA MENAL MUNTASEREEN.\nThen We caused the earth to swallow him up and his abode; then for him there was no group to help him against God; nor was he of those who can defend themselves.\nوَاَصْبَحَ الَّذِيْنَ تَمَنَّوْا مَكَانَهٗ بِالْاَمْسِ يَقُوْلُوْنَ وَيْكَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ وَيَقْدِرُ‌ۚ لَوْلَاۤ اَنْ مَّنَّ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْنَا لَخَسَفَ بِنَا‌ ؕ وَيْكَاَنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(82)\nWA ASBAHAL LAZEENA TAMANNAW MAKAANAHU BIL-AMSE YAQOOLOONA WAYKA-ANNAL LAAHA YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAYN YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI WA YAQDER, LAWLAA AM MANNAL LAAHO A’LAYNAA LAKHASAFA BENAA, WAYKA-ANNAHU LAA YUFLEHUL KAAFEROON.\nAnd those who coveted his position only the day before began saying: “Ah! that God amplifieth the sustenance for whomsoever He pleaseth, of his servants and straiteneth it; had not God been gracious unto us, He would certainly have abased us; Ah! the ungrateful (ones) succeed not.\nتِلْكَ الدَّارُ الْاٰخِرَةُ نَجْعَلُهَا لِلَّذِيْنَ لَا يُرِيْدُوْنَ عُلُوًّا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا فَسَادًا‌ ؕ وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(83)\nTILKAD DAARUL AAKHERATO NAJ-A’LOHAA LILLAZEENA LAA YOREEDOONA O’LUWWAN FIL ARZE WA LAA FASAADAA, WAL A-A’QEBATO LILMUTTAQEEN.\nThat abode in the hereafter, We assign it for those who intend not to exult themselves in the earth, nor (to make) mischief (therein) and the end is (best) for the pious ones.\nمَنْ جَآءَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ فَلَهٗ خَيْرٌ مِّنْهَا‌ ۚ وَمَنْ جَآءَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ فَلَا يُجْزَى الَّذِيْنَ عَمِلُوا السَّيِّاٰتِ اِلَّا مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(84)\nMAN JAAA-A BIL HASANATE FALAHU KHAYRUM MINHAA, WA MAN JAAA-A BISSAYYEATE FALAA YUJZAL LAZEENA A’MELUS SAYYE-AATE ILLAA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nWhosoever bringeth good, for him shall be better than it, and whosoever bringeth evil, then shall not be recompensed those who wrought evil, (with) aught save what they had been working.\nاِنَّ الَّذِىْ فَرَضَ عَلَيْكَ الْقُرْاٰنَ لَرَآدُّكَ اِلٰى مَعَادٍ‌ ؕ قُلْ رَّبِّىْۤ اَعْلَمُ مَنْ جَآءَ بِالْهُدٰى وَمَنْ هُوَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(85)\nINNAL LAZEE FARAZA A’LAYKAL QURAANA LARAAAD-DOKA ELAA MA-A’AD, QUR RABBEE A-A’LAMO MAN JAAA-A BILHODAA WA MAN HOWA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nVerily He Who hath ordained the Qur’an unto thee certainly bringeth thee back {to thy) home; Say thou: “My Lord knoweth best him who hath brought the guidance and him who is in manifest error.\nوَمَا كُنْتَ تَرْجُوْۤا اَنْ يُّلْقٰٓى اِلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبُ اِلَّا رَحْمَةً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ‌ فَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ ظَهِيْرًا لِّلْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(86)\nWA MAA KUNTA TARJOO AYN YULQAA ELAYKAL KETAABO ILLAA RAHMATAM MIR RABBEKA FALAA TAKOONANNA ZAHEERAL LIL KAAFEREEN.\nAnd thou didst not expect that the Book would be inspired unto thee, but it is a mercy from thy Lord, therefore be not a supporter of the disbelievers.\nوَلَا يَصُدُّنَّكَ عَنْ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ بَعْدَ اِذْ اُنْزِلَتْ اِلَيْكَ‌ وَادْعُ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ‌ وَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(87)\nWA LAA YASUDDUNNAKA A’N AAYAATIL LAAHE BA’DA IZ UNZELAT ELAYKA WAD-O’ ELAA RABBEKA WA LAA TAKOONANNA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nAnd let them not turn thee aside from the signs of God after they have been sent down unto thee, and call (mankind) unto thy Lord, and be not of the polytheists.\nوَلَا تَدْعُ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ‌ۘ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ‌ كُلُّ شَىْءٍ هَالِكٌ اِلَّا وَجْهَهٗ‌ؕ لَهُ الْحُكْمُ وَاِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(88)\nWA LAA TAD-O’ MA-A’L LAAHE ELAAHAN AAKHAR, LAA ELAAH ILLAA HOO, KULLO SHAY-IN HAALEKUN ILLAA WAJHAH, LAHUL HUKMO WA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nAnd call not with God any other god; There is no god but He: All things are perishable but He: His is the Authority, and unto Him shall ye be returned.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Qasas (The Narrative)\nThere are 88 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah though some scholars say that it was revealed in Madinah. The 58th verse of this Surah was revealed at the time of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.)’s migration from Makkah to Madinah.\nIt is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that whoever recites this Surah will get the reward equivalent to the number of people present at the time of Prophet Musa (a.s.) and all the angels will bear witness on his behalf. If one drinks the water in which this Surah has been dissolved, all his problems and worries will be solved.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved is a remedy from illness and worries (this can also be done by writing the Surah inside a container and then gathering rain water in the same container)."
